            <ArticleTitle>[Changes in the animal behavior caused by sequential changes of dominants related to reproduction].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>979-86</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Female rats during the sex dominanta (proestrus) revealed lower anxiety scores and a higher general level of activity than the rats in diestrus. Responses to stress were also more obvious in proestrus. During gestation the rats revealed a lower activity and a higher anxiety. In lactation, the rats' behaviour was similar to that in proestrus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
